<https://w3id.org/lmodel/attack/attack> dcterms:license "Apache-2.0" ;
	dcterms:source "https://github.com/mitre-attack/attack-stix-data/releases/tag/v20.0"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	dcterms:title "MITRE ATT&CK" ;
	pav:version "20.0" ;
	a linkml:SchemaDefinition ;
	rdfs:seeAlso "https://attack.mitre.org/resources/versions/"^^xsd:anyURI , "https://lmodel.github.io/attack"^^xsd:anyURI , "https://mitre-attack.github.io/attack-data-model/schemas/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "Some of the ADM's rules are beyond the validator, such as the order of a list or a rule across a bundle. tests/attack_rules.py checks them over the examples and the bundles, and docs/index.md lists them; the annotations attack_id_pattern, attack_domains, attack_excluded_domains and attack_tactic give the values those rules read." , "The ATT&CK Data Model (ADM), mitre-attack/attack-data-model, defines the STIX extensions ATT&CK uses. MITRE marks every release of its v4.11 line as a pre-release, published under npm's next tag, while npm's latest is v4.10.1. The schema follows v4.11.7 all the same, because the schema fixes of v4.11.1 to v4.11.6 match the v20.0 data, which post-dates them." , "The schema follows the data MITRE publishes. Where the v20.0 data departs from the ADM, the schema accepts the data, and tests/test_upstream.py lists each departure with its reason." , "The version is the ATT&CK release the schema renders, and source is that release of mitre-attack/attack-stix-data, at the commit in the annotations. tests/data/attack-stix-data/manifest.json pins its bundles by hash, and scripts/check_upstream_release.py reports a newer release." ;
	sh:declare _:c14n284 , _:c14n3 , _:c14n546 ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n178 , _:c14n205 , _:c14n352 , _:c14n370 , _:c14n468 , _:c14n508 ;
